#
# Conformance case: profiles/probabilistic-no-model
# AC (#506): probabilistic inference REQUIRES a declared independence/dependency
# model. Here a probabilistic fact (rain=0.5) is present but NO
# `:- probability_model(...)` is declared. The evaluator must REFUSE — returning
# status "unknown" with no bindings — rather than silently assuming independence.
# A computed marginal here would be the named failure mode (treating un-modelled
# probabilistic facts as if independence had been declared).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/profiles/probabilistic-no-model/> .

ex:Condition a logic:Kind .
